    <briefdescription>
<para>Concept satisfied when the tag of a comparator or of a predicate has a symbol that can be written. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Satisfied when the tag has a static member <computeroutput>symbol</computeroutput> that the formatter can write. Used by <computeroutput>reject_compare_tag()</computeroutput> and by <computeroutput>reject_predicate_tag()</computeroutput>, to tell a missing or unprintable symbol from a wrong <computeroutput>apply()</computeroutput>.</para>
